          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10.2 The Token Model"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.162,
            0.467,
            0.183
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Using tokens for addition"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.191,
            0.886,
            0.326
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In Bela’s Building of Fun, the lift attendant is bored. To entertain himself, he keeps a box containing lots of positive (green) and negative (red) tokens. Each time he presses the ‘+’ button, he takes a positive token from the box and puts it in his pocket. Similarly, each time he presses the ‘–’ button, he takes a negative token and puts it in his pocket."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.328,
            0.885,
            0.394
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "He starts on the ground floor (Floor 0) with an empty pocket. After one hour, he checks his pocket and finds 5 positive and 3 negative tokens. On which floor is he now?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.396,
            0.882,
            0.439
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "He must have pressed ‘+’ five times and ‘–’ 3 times and (+ 5)+(– 3)= + 2. So, he is at Floor + 2 now."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.194,
            0.442,
            0.632,
            0.462
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Here is another way to do the calculation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.38,
            0.477,
            0.664,
            0.573
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.38,
                0.477,
                0.664,
                0.573
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_14_image_7.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.583,
            0.886,
            0.718
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A positive token and a negative token cancel each other, because the value of this pair of tokens together is zero. These two tokens in his pocket meant that he pressed ‘+’ once and ‘–’ once, respectively, and these cancel each other. We say that a positive and a negative token make a ʻzero pairʼ. When you remove all the zero pairs, you are left with two positive tokens, so (+5) + (–3) = +2."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.194,
            0.72,
            0.712,
            0.741
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We can perform any such addition using tokens!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.755,
            0.442,
            0.776
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Add + 5 and – 8."
            }
          ]
        },
